course: dictionary
lesson: 15686
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it show you which one you need. The word times is a good example. «Five times six is thirty» uses times with numbers, so it means multiplied, not a period of history or a clock.
explain: «She times the race with a stopwatch.» Here times is a verb. To time something means to measure how long it takes. The word stopwatch is your clue. Always ask: which meaning fits these words?
explain: «In old times, people had no phones.» Here times means a period in history. The word old is the clue. Try a different meaning in the sentence and see whether it still makes sense.
fact: Times can be a noun, a preposition or a verb, so check how it is used in the sentence.
fact: «5 times 6» means 5 × 6, which is 30: five groups of six put together.
fact: «I rang 4 times» means I rang on four occasions, so times tells how often something happens.
fact: «At times» means sometimes, and «three times a day» means three times in each day.
fact: «Behind the times» means old-fashioned, and «good times» in casual talk means a fun time.
exercise: «Five times six is thirty.» What does times mean here? | To measure how long something takes | A period in history | *Multiplied by, so five groups of six
exercise: «She times the race with a stopwatch.» What does times mean here? | *To measure how long something takes | How often something happens | Periods in history
exercise: «I rang the bell 4 times.» What does times tell us in this sentence? | A multiplying sign | To measure how long | *How often something happened
test: «In old times, people had no phones.» What does times mean here? | *A period in history | To measure how long | Multiplied by
test: «Three times as many children came to the party.» What does times mean here? | To measure a race | *Three copies of the number, so three groups | Now and again, sometimes
exam: A maths question says «increase threefold». What does this mean? | Take away three from it | Add three to it | Share it into three equal parts | *Multiply it by three
